OL,3,GNEWSABrighton's West Pier and its
OL,4,Abattle with nature
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Anthea Secker learned another
OL,7,Fsection of Brighton's West Pier had
OL,8,Fcollapsed into the sea, she said she
OL,9,Fwas devastated.
OL,11,FThe West Pier has become one of the
OL,12,Fcity's most recognisable landmarks -
OL,13,Fthe rugged lines of its metal skeleton
OL,14,Fhave become a familiar part of the
OL,15,Fcity's skyline, alongside the seagull
OL,16,Fand the Royal Pavilion.
OL,18,FNow, as more storm damage weakens its
OL,19,Fstructure and sends more pieces
OL,20,Funderwater, residents are reflecting on
OL,21,Fwhat the pier means to Brighton and
OL,22,Fwhat its future may hold.
OL,23,APub: 01-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,329,320,200,140,0,100
